# BEGIN public-boundary guard (generated by tools/check-public-boundary.py --sync-gitignore)
# Source of truth: docs/internal/public-private-boundary.md
# Repo kind: product-fork
# Ignore rules are defence in depth only. `git add -f` defeats .gitignore, and .gitignore never applies to an already-tracked path. The blocking guarantee comes from the installed pre-commit / pre-merge-commit / pre-push hooks.
# PB-001 Private test roots
/tests/
/private-tests/
/sloptank-tests/
/hidden-tests/
/private/
